{"title":"Career Roadmap · GIS Analyst","role":"GIS Analyst","summary":"A BA in Geography provides a strong foundation for spatial thinking, human and physical geography, cartography, regional analysis and geographic information systems. It is a good foundation for GIS Analyst roles, but the degree alone is not enough for most technical GIS positions.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should deliberately add GIS software, spatial databases, remote sensing, cartography, spatial analysis and basic programming during the degree."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong modern profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Geography","GIS","Remote Sensing","Spatial Data","Python","SQL/PostGIS","Web GIS"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build geography, cartography and GIS fundamentals; develop ArcGIS/QGIS and spatial-analysis skills"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Enter GIS Analyst, GIS Technician, Mapping Analyst, Geospatial Analyst or Remote Sensing roles"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to Senior GIS Analyst, Geospatial Specialist, GIS Developer or Spatial Data Analyst"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"GIS Lead, Geospatial Solutions Architect, GIS Manager, Remote Sensing Lead or Geospatial Consultant"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the BA","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The key combination should be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Geography","GIS","Cartography","Spatial Analysis","Remote Sensing","Data Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Geography Foundation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical geography"},{"text":"Human geography"},{"text":"Economic geography"},{"text":"Urban geography"},{"text":"Population geography"},{"text":"Environmental geography"},{"text":"Regional geography"},{"text":"Development geography"},{"text":"Climatology"},{"text":"Geomorphology"},{"text":"Hydrology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GIS Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Coordinate systems"},{"text":"Projections"},{"text":"Spatial data"},{"text":"Vector data"},{"text":"Raster data"},{"text":"Georeferencing"},{"text":"Digitisation"},{"text":"Spatial queries"},{"text":"Spatial joins"},{"text":"Buffering"},{"text":"Overlay analysis"},{"text":"Network analysis"},{"text":"Map design"},{"text":"Geospatial databases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Geography & Mapping Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic focus"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical geography"},{"text":"Human geography"},{"text":"Regional geography"},{"text":"Cartography"},{"text":"Map interpretation"},{"text":"Statistics for geography"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"Basic ArcGIS concepts"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Basic GPS concepts"},{"text":"Coordinate systems"},{"text":"Latitude/longitude"},{"text":"Map projections"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"District population map"},{"text":"Land-use map"},{"text":"Road-network map"},{"text":"Elevation map"},{"text":"Urban growth map"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to learn the complete process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Data","Processing","Analysis","Map","Interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — GIS & Spatial Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"This should become the student's major technical-development year."},{"type":"h","text":"GIS skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vector analysis"},{"text":"Raster analysis"},{"text":"Spatial joins"},{"text":"Geoprocessing"},{"text":"Buffer analysis"},{"text":"Overlay analysis"},{"text":"Proximity analysis"},{"text":"Network analysis"},{"text":"Terrain analysis"},{"text":"Spatial statis